    'terms_provider_text' => "PRODEX is the trade name under which the software-as-a-service (SaaS) platform described in these Terms of Service (the \"Terms\") is offered, operated at the domain prodexhub.cloud (the \"Site\") and accessed through the subdomains assigned to each business customer (the \"Service\").\n\nUnless expressly stated otherwise on this same page, the legal owner of the PRODEX brand and the party responsible for providing the Service (the \"Provider,\" \"we,\" or \"PRODEX\") is the natural or legal person identified in Section 30 (Contact) of this document. You may request, at any time, the full legal identification of the Provider (legal/registered name, registered address, and tax identification number, where applicable) by writing to the contact address listed in Section 30; that identification will be added to this document as soon as it is confirmed.\n\nThese Terms govern exclusively the relationship between the Provider and the user regarding use of the Service. For subscriptions where Paddle.com Market Limited (\"Paddle\") acts as the Merchant of Record, the sale of the right to use the Service and the processing of payment are additionally governed by Paddle's buyer terms, as explained in Section 19.",

    'terms_definitions_text' => "For the purposes of these Terms, the following terms have the meaning set out below:\n\n\"Account\": the record that identifies a business customer and its users within the Service.\n\n\"Customer,\" \"you,\" or \"User\": the natural or legal person that contracts the Service, and any person that business authorizes to access the Account.\n\n\"Customer Data\": all information, files, records, and content that the Customer or its Users upload, generate, or store within the Service, including without limitation inventory, sales, customer, supplier, employee, and reporting data.\n\n\"Tenant\" or \"Workspace\": the logically isolated environment within PRODEX's multi-tenant infrastructure assigned to each Customer, with its own database.\n\n\"Plan\": the service tier, features, and usage limits contracted by the Customer, as described on the Site's pricing page in effect at the time of contracting.\n\n\"Subscription\": the agreement for continued provision of the Service in exchange for the periodic payment corresponding to the chosen Plan.\n\n\"Billing Period\": the monthly or annual interval on which the Subscription is charged.\n\n\"Paddle\": Paddle.com Market Limited and its affiliates, a payment provider that acts as Merchant of Record for certain Service transactions, as described in Section 19.",

    'terms_capacity_text' => "By creating an Account, you represent and warrant that: (a) you are at least 18 years old or of legal age in your jurisdiction; (b) you have full legal capacity to enter into a binding contract; and (c) if you are creating the Account on behalf of a company, organization, or other entity, you have the authority necessary to bind that entity to these Terms, and references to \"you\" or \"Customer\" thereafter include that entity.\n\nPRODEX is designed primarily for business (B2B) use. However, if you legally qualify as a consumer under your jurisdiction with respect to this contract, nothing in these Terms is intended to deprive you of any non-waivable rights that status grants you under applicable law.\n\nThe Customer is responsible for all actions taken under its Account by anyone it authorizes to access it (employees, contractors, advisors, or other third parties), and for ensuring that such persons comply with these Terms. PRODEX does not independently verify the identity, authority, or employment relationship of internal Users the Customer registers.",

    'terms_multitenancy_text' => "PRODEX operates on a multi-tenant architecture: each business customer receives a logically isolated Workspace with its own database, so that one company's Customer Data is not accessible to other companies using the Service.\n\nWithin a given Workspace, the Customer is responsible for configuring the roles, permissions, and access levels of its own internal Users. PRODEX provides the technical access-control tools, but the decision of who gets which permissions rests exclusively with the Customer.\n\nMulti-tenant isolation is a reasonable technical data-separation measure; on its own it does not constitute an absolute guarantee of security against every conceivable scenario, as further described in Section 20 (Security).",

    'terms_plans_pricing_text' => "Available Plans, their features, usage limits, and prices are published on the Site's pricing page and may be updated from time to time. The price applicable to your Subscription is the one in effect at the time of contracting or of the corresponding renewal, unless a specific promotion states otherwise.\n\nIf PRODEX changes the price of a Plan, that change does not affect the Billing Period already in progress; it applies starting with the next renewal, and we will notify you with reasonable advance notice through the contact channels associated with your Account when the change is material.\n\nPrices are shown in the currency indicated on the Site or during the contracting process. When payment is processed through Paddle, the exact amount to be charged, any currency conversion, and applicable taxes will be calculated and displayed by Paddle at checkout before the payment is confirmed, based on the tax rules of the buyer's billing country. PRODEX does not control Paddle's currency conversion rates or tax policies.\n\nYou are responsible for keeping your Account's billing information (including, where applicable, your tax details) up to date so that issued invoices are correct.",

    'terms_trial_text' => "The Emprendedor (Starter) Plan currently includes, subject to change, a free trial period that does not require a payment method to begin evaluating it. The exact trial length that applies to your signup is the one shown during registration or on the pricing page at the time you start the trial; under Paddle's current configuration for the Emprendedor Plan, that period is up to 30 days.\n\nIf a payment method is requested during registration to activate the trial (for example, when the trial is managed through Paddle), you will not be charged during the trial period. When the trial ends, the Subscription automatically activates on the selected Plan and billing cycle and periodic billing begins, unless you cancelled before the trial ended in accordance with Section 12.\n\nPRODEX may modify, limit, or withdraw the availability of free trials for new signups at any time, without affecting trials already in progress.",

    'terms_billing_failures_text' => "By contracting a paid Subscription, you authorize PRODEX (or, where applicable, Paddle in its capacity as Merchant of Record, or the payment provider you chose) to recurringly charge the payment method associated with your Account, in accordance with the Plan and Billing Period in effect, until the Subscription is cancelled under Section 12.\n\nIf a charge cannot be completed (for example, due to insufficient funds, an expired card, or issuer decline), the relevant payment provider may retry the charge according to its own retry (\"dunning\") policies. While retries are pending, your Subscription may move into a suspended state: in that state, access to the Service's features is restricted until payment is resolved, without this being equivalent to cancellation of the Subscription.\n\nIf payment is not resolved within a reasonable period, PRODEX may cancel the Subscription for non-payment. PRODEX does not currently offer a formal grace period with guaranteed full access beyond what the payment retry cycle itself allows; if a formal grace period is implemented in the future, it will be expressly described in this document before it takes effect.",

    'terms_cancellation_text' => "You may cancel auto-renewal of your Subscription at any time from your Account dashboard or by requesting it from support, through the contact channels in Section 30.\n\nA scheduled cancellation does NOT interrupt your access immediately: you retain full access to the Service through the end of the Billing Period you already paid for. From that date onward, no further charge will be generated and access is suspended, unless you reactivate the Subscription before that date under Section 13.\n\nAmounts for Billing Periods already charged before cancellation are not refunded simply because you cancelled, without prejudice to the refund scenarios described in the Refund & Cancellation Policy and any non-waivable right you may have under law.",

    'terms_resumption_text' => "If you cancelled auto-renewal but your Subscription has not yet reached the end of the paid Billing Period, you can resume it from your Account dashboard or by requesting it from support. Resuming before that date restores auto-renewal and the Service continues without interruption, provided that is technically possible under the rules of the payment provider used (for example, Paddle) at the time of the request.\n\nIf the Subscription has already been confirmed as cancelled or ended (for example, because the Billing Period already concluded or the payment provider confirmed the final cancellation), resumption is not possible and you will need to contract a new Subscription.\n\nIf your Subscription is suspended due to a payment issue (Section 11) rather than a scheduled cancellation, resuming or removing the scheduled cancellation does not by itself restore access; you must first resolve the outstanding payment issue.",

    'terms_refunds_ref_text' => "The conditions under which a charge may be refunded (including billing errors, duplicate charges, unrecognized charges, and severe Service unavailability attributable to PRODEX) are set out in full in our Refund & Cancellation Policy, which is an integral part of these Terms and prevails over this section in the event of a conflict regarding that specific subject matter.",

    'terms_customer_data_text' => "As between the Customer and PRODEX, the Customer retains ownership of all Customer Data. PRODEX does not claim any ownership rights over that data. PRODEX holds only the technical license strictly necessary to store, process, back up, and display Customer Data for the purpose of providing the Service, including any technical support the Customer requests.\n\nWhen the Customer uploads personal data of third parties into the Service (for example, of its own customers, employees, or suppliers), the Customer acts under its own responsibility and is the party that determines the purpose of such processing; the Customer represents that it holds the authorizations, notices, or legal bases that applicable data-protection law requires to enter that information into the Service. How PRODEX handles personal data, and the distinction between data PRODEX processes on its own behalf and data it processes on the Customer's instructions, are described in the Privacy Policy.\n\nWhile your Account is active, you may export your Customer Data using the export tools available in the Service. After Account termination, Customer Data is retained and subsequently deleted according to the retention periods described in the Privacy Policy; we recommend exporting any information you need before the Account is deleted.",

    'terms_availability_text' => "PRODEX works to keep the Service available on a continuous basis, but the Service is provided \"as is\" and \"as available,\" to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law. We do not guarantee that the Service will operate without interruption, fully uninterrupted, error-free, or that it will produce any particular business outcome.\n\nWe may perform scheduled or emergency maintenance, updates, improvements, and changes to the Service's features at any time. Where reasonably possible, we will try to give advance notice of maintenance likely to cause a significant interruption.\n\nWe may occasionally offer features marked as beta, experimental, or preview. Such features are provided without additional warranties, may change or be discontinued without notice, and should not be considered a stable part of the contracted Plan until released generally.\n\nWe maintain backups of Customer Data as part of our internal operational practices, as a business-continuity measure; those backups do not replace the Customer's responsibility to export and externally safeguard any information it considers critical.",

    'terms_integrations_text' => "The Service may integrate with, or depend on, third-party providers and services, including payment processors, messaging services, cloud infrastructure providers, and other business tools. PRODEX does not control and is not responsible for the operation, availability, policies, or changes of such third parties, except to the extent applicable law provides otherwise.\n\nFor certain Subscriptions, PRODEX uses Paddle.com Market Limited (\"Paddle\") as Merchant of Record. In those cases, Paddle — not PRODEX — is the party that sells the Subscription, processes the payment, issues the tax invoice for that transaction, and is responsible to you for that sale process, under Paddle's buyer terms. PRODEX remains solely responsible for providing the Service (the software) itself. Nothing in these Terms should be read as copying, replacing, or modifying Paddle's terms; in the event of a conflict regarding the payment transaction processed by Paddle, Paddle's terms applicable to that transaction prevail.\n\nThe Service may contain links to external sites or resources. Such links are provided solely for convenience and do not imply any endorsement by PRODEX of their content.",

    'terms_security_text' => "PRODEX implements reasonable technical and organizational measures, consistent with common practices in the software-as-a-service industry, to protect the Service and Customer Data against unauthorized access, loss, or alteration. No security measure is absolute or can guarantee protection against every possible incident.\n\nThe Customer is responsible for: (a) keeping its access credentials confidential; (b) properly configuring the roles and permissions of its internal Users; (c) notifying PRODEX without undue delay of any suspected unauthorized access to its Account; and (d) implementing, in its own environment (devices, networks, endpoints), the reasonable security measures that fall to it as a user of the Service.",

    'terms_fiscal_text' => "PRODEX is a business-management tool (point of sale, inventory, sales, purchasing, operational invoicing, and related modules) that helps you record and organize your business information. Using PRODEX, by itself, does not relieve you of any tax, accounting, labor, commercial, or regulatory obligation applicable to your business under the law of your country or of any country where you operate.\n\nYou are solely responsible for verifying that your configuration and use of PRODEX (including how you record sales, issue receipts, calculate taxes applicable to your own operations, and keep your own records) satisfies the tax, accounting, and regulatory obligations specific to your business, including any electronic-invoicing, tax-authorization, receipt-numbering, or other special-regime requirement your jurisdiction may impose. PRODEX is not designed to automatically determine what your tax obligations are, nor to file returns or receipts with any tax authority on your behalf, unless a specific integration expressly states so and you have configured that integration.\n\nPRODEX does not replace the judgment of a certified public accountant, auditor, lawyer, or tax advisor. We recommend consulting your own professional advisors to confirm that your intended use of the platform satisfies your specific legal obligations before relying on it for that purpose.",

    'terms_warranties_text' => "To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Service is provided \"as is\" and \"as available,\" without warranties of any kind, whether express, implied, or statutory, including, without limitation, implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, or non-infringement.\n\nPRODEX does not warrant that: (a) the Service will meet all of your specific requirements; (b) the Service will operate uninterrupted, timely, securely, or error-free; (c) results obtained through use of the Service will be accurate or reliable for any particular purpose; or (d) errors in the Service will be corrected within any particular timeframe.\n\nNothing in this section is intended to exclude any warranty that applicable law does not permit to be excluded; in that case, the relevant warranty is limited to the minimum extent permitted by that law.",

    'terms_indemnification_text' => "To the extent permitted by applicable law, you agree to defend, indemnify, and hold harmless PRODEX, its directors, employees, contractors, and suppliers, from and against any claim, demand, damage, loss, liability, cost, and expense (including reasonable legal fees) arising out of or related to: (a) misuse of the Service by you or your internal Users; (b) your breach of these Terms; (c) the Customer Data you upload, including any third-party claim related to the lack of legal authorization to process their personal data within your Workspace; or (d) your failure to comply with the tax, accounting, or regulatory obligations described in Section 21.\n\nThis indemnification obligation does not apply to the extent the claim arises from a breach, gross negligence, or willful misconduct directly attributable to PRODEX. PRODEX reserves the right to assume sole control of the defense of any indemnifiable matter, in which case you will cooperate reasonably with that defense.",

    'terms_force_majeure_text' => "Neither party will be liable for any failure or delay in performing its obligations (other than payment obligations) where that failure or delay is caused by circumstances reasonably beyond its control, including, without limitation: natural disasters, fires, floods, acts of government, war, civil unrest, strikes, widespread internet or telecommunications infrastructure failures, large-scale cyberattacks not attributable to a PRODEX security failure, or failures of cloud infrastructure providers outside PRODEX's control.",

    'terms_termination_text' => "You may terminate your relationship with PRODEX at any time by cancelling your Subscription under Section 12 and, if you wish, requesting deletion of your Account.\n\nPRODEX may suspend or terminate your access to the Service, immediately where the severity of the case warrants it, when: (a) you materially breach these Terms; (b) your use of the Service poses a security, legal, or fraud risk to PRODEX, other Customers, or third parties; (c) you have overdue payments that remain unresolved under Section 11; or (d) required by law or a competent authority. Where reasonably possible and the severity of the case allows, we will try to notify you before terminating for breach.\n\nUpon termination of your Account: (a) your right to access and use the Service ends; (b) the provisions of these Terms that by their nature should survive (including, without limitation, intellectual property, limitation of liability, indemnification, governing law, and the sections addressing the subsequent handling of your data) will continue in effect; and (c) your Customer Data will be retained and subsequently deleted according to the retention periods described in the Privacy Policy.",

    'terms_changes_text' => "We may update these Terms from time to time to reflect changes in the Service, our business practices, or applicable law. The current version will always be available on this page, along with its last-updated date.\n\nWhen a change is material (that is, it significantly reduces your rights or significantly expands your obligations), we will try to notify you with reasonable advance notice through the contact channels associated with your Account or through a visible notice within the Service, before the change takes effect. Continued use of the Service after the effective date of an update constitutes your acceptance of the updated Terms; if you do not agree with a material change, your remedy is to cancel your Subscription before that change takes effect.",

