    'privacy_contact_title'       => '18. Contact',

    'privacy_roles_text' => "This Privacy Policy distinguishes between two different situations, because PRODEX's role is not the same in each:\n\n(A) Data PRODEX processes to manage its own relationship with you as a PRODEX customer. This is the account data you create to contract and manage the Service: your name, email address, company information, billing details, and communications with our support or sales team. With respect to this data, PRODEX determines what it is used for (providing the Service, billing you, supporting you, complying with legal obligations) and, in that sense, decides the purposes and means of processing.\n\n(B) Data your business enters into PRODEX about its own customers, employees, suppliers, or other individuals, while using the Service's modules (for example, a sales record containing a buyer's name, or an employee's file in the HR module). With respect to this data, it is your business — not PRODEX — that decides why it is collected and what is done with it; PRODEX only stores and processes it to the extent strictly necessary to operate the Service your business configured and uses, following your instructions (for example, displaying that data when you log in, generating the reports you request, or performing the corresponding technical backups).\n\nDepending on the data-protection law that applies to you, this functional distinction may correspond, with nuances, to concepts such as \"controller\" and \"processor\" (or their local equivalents), without this implying that PRODEX claims to be subject to a specific regulatory regime that does not apply to it. If your business enters third-party personal data into PRODEX, it is you who must ensure you have the legal basis, consent, or privacy notice that applicable data-protection law requires with respect to those individuals; PRODEX has no visibility into, or control over, the relationship between your business and those individuals.",

    'privacy_technical_text' => "When you visit the Site or use the Service, we automatically collect certain technical information, including: IP address, browser type and version, operating system, device identifiers, pages visited, date and time of access, and activity logs relevant to the operation, security, and troubleshooting of the Service.\n\nWe use cookies and similar technologies (browser local storage, session identifiers) to keep you signed in, remember your preferences (such as language or cookie consent), and, where applicable and with your consent, for analytics on Site usage. Section 15 describes in more detail the categories of cookies used and how you can manage them.\n\nIf we enable third-party analytics tools on the Site, those tools may collect aggregated information about Site usage under their own privacy policies.",

    'privacy_customer_content_text' => "PRODEX includes modules (sales, inventory, customers, suppliers, invoicing, human resources, among others) designed so your business can record information about its own customers, employees, suppliers, or other individuals related to its operations. This information is stored within your isolated Workspace and is controlled by your business, not by PRODEX.\n\nPRODEX does not use this information for its own commercial purposes (for example, it does not use it for PRODEX's own marketing or share it with other Customers). PRODEX's technical access to this information is limited to what is necessary to provide the Service, provide technical support you request, perform backups, and comply with legal obligations or valid requests from a competent authority.\n\nIf your business stops using the Service, this information is retained and subsequently deleted according to the periods described in Section 12, unless you request its earlier deletion.",

    'privacy_legal_basis_text' => "Where applicable law requires identifying a legal basis for processing personal data, PRODEX processes the data described in Section 2(A) on the following bases, as applicable: (a) performance of a contract, when processing is necessary to provide the Service you contracted; (b) compliance with a legal obligation, for example, accounting, tax, or record-retention obligations; (c) legitimate interest, for example, to prevent fraud, maintain the security of the Service, or improve its operation, provided that interest does not override your fundamental rights; and (d) consent, when we expressly request it, for example, for certain non-essential cookies or marketing communications, which you may withdraw at any time without affecting the lawfulness of processing carried out before the withdrawal.\n\nWith respect to the data described in Section 2(B), the applicable legal basis depends on the relationship between your business and the individuals whose data you record, and it is your business that must determine it and, where applicable, document it.",

    'privacy_payments_text' => "When you contract a paid Subscription, we process the billing data necessary to issue invoices and administer your Account (for example, name or company name, billing email, and, where applicable, tax details).\n\nPRODEX does not store full credit or debit card numbers on its own servers. Processing of the payment itself (capturing your card or other payment method details, authorizing the charge, and, for certain Subscriptions, issuing the invoice for that transaction) is carried out directly by our payment provider, including Paddle.com Market Limited when it acts as Merchant of Record, under that provider's own privacy policy. We recommend reviewing Paddle's privacy policy to understand how it handles the data you provide directly during checkout.\n\nWe may receive from our payment provider limited information about the status of a transaction (for example, whether a payment succeeded, failed, or was refunded), and an identifier for the transaction or payment method (for example, the last four digits of a card) for reconciliation, support, and fraud-prevention purposes — not the full card number or its security data.",

    'privacy_third_party_text' => "We use service providers that process data on our behalf and under our instructions so we can operate the Service (\"sub-processors\" or \"providers\"), including: cloud infrastructure and hosting providers; transactional email delivery providers; Paddle, for payment processing and, when it acts as Merchant of Record, for the sale of the Subscription; and, when enabled, Site analytics and messaging tools (for example, the WhatsApp Business API) that your own business configures for its operations.\n\nWe contractually require our providers to handle data with reasonable confidentiality and security standards appropriate to the nature of the data, and to use it only to provide us the contracted service, not for their own commercial purposes unrelated to that service.",

    'privacy_international_text' => "PRODEX provides the Service primarily from cloud infrastructure that may be located outside your country, potentially including outside Honduras and Central America. By using the Service, your data and the Customer Data you record may be transferred, stored, and processed in those data centers.\n\nWhere applicable law requires additional safeguards for international transfers of personal data (for example, contractual clauses or equivalent mechanisms with our providers), we seek to ensure our infrastructure and payment providers maintain reasonable security standards and, where applicable, transfer mechanisms recognized under applicable law.",

    'privacy_retention_text' => "We retain your Account data and the Customer Data in your Workspace while your Subscription is active, and for a reasonable additional period after Account cancellation or termination, in order to: (a) allow you to reactivate your Account should you choose to; (b) comply with legal, accounting, or tax obligations that require retaining certain records for a minimum period; and (c) resolve disputes or enforce our agreements.\n\nAfter that period, we delete or anonymize data that is no longer necessary for the above purposes, unless the law requires a longer retention period. You may request early deletion of your Account and your data by writing to us through the contact channels in Section 18; we will act on that request to the extent no legal retention obligation prevents it.\n\nTechnical backups may retain copies of information for a limited additional period as a business-continuity measure, even after the information has been deleted from the production environment; those backups are overwritten as part of our normal operating cycle.",

    'privacy_minors_text' => "The Service is directed at businesses and at adults acting in a professional or business capacity. We do not direct the Service at minors and do not knowingly collect personal data from minors through the Account registration process. If you have reason to believe a minor has provided us with personal data through the registration process, please contact us so we can delete it.\n\nThis section does not apply to Customer Data that a business customer chooses to record about minors within its own modules (for example, a merchant recording a sale indirectly related to a minor); that processing is the sole responsibility of the business customer under Section 2(B) and the law applicable to it.",

    'privacy_external_links_text' => "The Site and the Service may contain links to third-party websites or services not operated by PRODEX (for example, Paddle's checkout, or links to social media). We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of such third-party sites. We recommend reviewing the privacy policy of any third-party site you visit through a link from our Service.",

    'privacy_changes_text' => "We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in the Service, our providers, or applicable law. We will post the current version on this page along with its last-updated date. When a change is material, we will try to notify you with reasonable advance notice through the contact channels associated with your Account or through a visible notice within the Service.",

